  {
    "episode_id": 70766,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70766.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 36,
    "turn_text": "What kind of guy was he? Oh man, you're going to make me cry. He was a great guy. I mean, he was the most amazing human being and kindest human being in the world. When I joined the unit in New Mexico, I was actually not in the best shape. I had messed up my knee and was not Well, I would say was not in the best shape to even go to war, but I was not also going to not go to war, like when you get your order to go. So John then actually lived fairly near me. And so prior to our activation, knowing that we're going to wreck, he would come by and we'd work out together and he'd help me get ready to be in the shape that I needed to do to go to war. Why did he decide to look at me like that? Well, because I had no friends. Like, I had just moved to New Mexico. I was alone. There was nobody, no one else to go work out with or anything else like that. And I think he, I think we just got along great. My son's named after him. He's been on his grant. And even throughout the war, when things started getting really heavy, he always had this smile on his face. He was just a kind-hearted guy. You still always steal my Nanopods, I don't know what the heck they were calling back. The old MP3 players loved my music. Guy can eat anything. And just one of those good human beings that you are very lucky to meet.",
