  {
    "episode_id": 70766,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70766.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 65,
    "turn_text": "Well, I mean, first you have to understand why we even think that way. I mean, so after those two days, we're lost about one third of my platoon, then we go back to our base and then we go back out I mean, they give us a couple days break, then we start going back out. And then every day, someone else, every other day, it's then felt like someone's either shooting at us or somebody died or somebody got hit or somebody's always trying to take, you know, try to take my life. And you'd see these IEDs that go off in the middle of like streets and surrounded by these houses. Like clearly somebody saw this. Clearly, you know, these Iraqi villagers could have told us or they could have like given us a warning. They had all these ways for them to actually call, and anonymously and give us tips. I remember when I, one of the first firefights I got into, I was going through this road along the river and all of a sudden everyone just disappeared. And as soon as that happened, They hit us with RPG and machine gun fire. And they had clearly set this up for quite a while. And they basically let us go into an ambush. So the way you think about this is they're not innocent. They're now part of the enemy, because they're helping out the enemy. And you just, when you're going through these crowds and I used to patrol through these crowded marketplaces, at any point, they could be there. And the search could be among those people and then you're going to get taken or taken out by one of these guys and these people aren't going to help you at all. And you feel angry. You start thinking them as the enemy. And the way that I kind of got myself out of it is just I try to give myself some rules. And the two rules was that I was going to survive. And when I didn't think I was going to be able to survive, that I was going Go honorably, and",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
