    "turn_text": "Part of the other things that helped me think about this is that as a Marine, if I committed a war crime, it would give me personal satisfaction, but only make the job more difficult for the rest of the men in my unit. And if you're a Marine, the first thing they teach you is mission objective, right? And war crime is by nature horrible because you're targeting innocent civilians and basically going against basic rules of humanity. But it also will endanger your mission, endanger your men. And I think if you're someone like as Iranians or President Trump, you really need to think about that. What is the mission here? The mission of Iran is pretty simple. Get the United States out of Iraq, make Iraq a proxy state, so that way Iran can control from Tehran all the way to the Mediterranean and Swathiland that they've always wanted to control. Our objective should be to have a stable secular Iraq that is a buffer to Iran. Right now, if President Trump is smart, and find out pretty soon. Our goal is to make sure that we have a ally in Iraq and not seek revenge and not allow the Iranians to have their goals met. And if they keep that in mind instead of the idea of like revenge on a revenge, I think, you know, we as United States could probably be in a better position.",
