    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/0/70766.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 125,
    "turn_text": "Of course, I mean, it's a hard situation we're talking about. So a base being fired on with no intent to kill anybody is probably an opportunity for us to de-escalate this. So as I was telling you, I always saw it as a massive base. And we pretty sure that there was a heads up that this was coming. And hopefully this is the time of de-escalate. But what I'm trying to say is that we go to war with Iran, and it's not going to be a bunch of men and women facing off on a line. The way Iran is going to hurt us is they're just going to use their proxies all over the world, terrorist actions to basically put such a terror and fear as well as just cyber attacks, all these other things that are just basically going to harm us in ways that we are not going to be able to stop. And that's why people, in my opinion, aren't getting this idea of World War III.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
